(2399454, 329005, 30861, '<td valign="top">WTG Sheryl! Terrific backdrop to this one, really impressed me.</td>', 'WTG Sheryl! Terrific backdrop to this one, really impressed me.', '2006-05-10 02:18:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2399463, 329005, 48228, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, as you are the only one that saw this, as I delibrately put the "purple" colored pencil out of place, re the color wheel, to see if someone would pick up on it, and you did.....<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tngrndream:</b></div><hr/><i> that one (the purple one) looks like it is in the wrong place. was that intentional. or is it just supposed to be that way. at any rate, it draws my eyes right to it and forces me to remain in the composition. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Congratulations, as you are the only one that saw this, as I delibrately put the "purple" colored pencil out of place, re the color wheel, to see if someone would pick up on it, and you did..... Originally posted by tngrndream: that one (the purple one) looks like it is in the wrong place. was that intentional. or is it just supposed to be that way. at any rate, it draws my eyes right to it and forces me to remain in the composition. ', '2006-05-10 02:21:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2399490, 329141, 30861, '<td valign="top">Happy to see this make top 10 :-) Congrats!</td>', 'Happy to see this make top 10 :-) Congrats!', '2006-05-10 02:27:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2399509, 329005, 48228, '<td valign="top">Now for all the others who commented on my background. Most loved it but many said that they would prefer a flat black background and not the corrugated "textured" one that I used. The reason why I used this in preference to a flat black one is answered in two sentences. <br/> <br/>First of all I tried the flat black background and the the flat one lost some of the "rhythm" that I wanted to achieve.<br/> <br/>Secondly, I love texture, so I personally love the one I chose. I also found that the corrugated card held the rolling pencils in place , so that was a bonus.....<br/> <br/>Thank you everyone for commenting and voting on my image.....<br/> <br/>All I can say now is "Watch out to those who beat me to my first ribbon, as I now have the taste for it, and will be trying much harder to achieve my dream".</td>', 'Now for all the others who commented on my background. Most loved it but many said that they would prefer a flat black background and not the corrugated "textured" one that I used. The reason why I used this in preference to a flat black one is answered in two sentences.  First of all I tried the flat black background and the the flat one lost some of the "rhythm" that I wanted to achieve. Secondly, I love texture, so I personally love the one I chose. I also found that the corrugated card held the rolling pencils in place , so that was a bonus..... Thank you everyone for commenting and voting on my image..... All I can say now is "Watch out to those who beat me to my first ribbon, as I now have the taste for it, and will be trying much harder to achieve my dream".', '2006-05-10 02:31:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2399519, 327280, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Top ten, extremely well deserved.   Congratulations on your new excellent work in "Up, up and away" this is an amazing piece in the Rhythm II challenge.  <br/> <br/>The overall image just grabs your attention.  The pattern is obviously are very interesting, especially from this angle.  At first glance I thought Jenja (that game where you stack the wooden blocks) but upon closer look realized it was a very intricate building.  The composition is just wonderful, placing this subject just off of center works for me. <br/> <br/>It must have been a sunny day to capture the much sun from the left side.  The sunlight really brings out the pattern, great job! I look forward to your future entries.</td>', '*Critique Club* Top ten, extremely well deserved.   Congratulations on your new excellent work in "Up, up and away" this is an amazing piece in the Rhythm II challenge.   The overall image just grabs your attention.  The pattern is obviously are very interesting, especially from this angle.  At first glance I thought Jenja (that game where you stack the wooden blocks) but upon closer look realized it was a very intricate building.  The composition is just wonderful, placing this subject just off of center works for me.  It must have been a sunny day to capture the much sun from the left side.  The sunlight really brings out the pattern, great job! I look forward to your future entries.', '2006-05-10 02:35:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2399581, 329353, 51988, '<td valign="top">Great shot Cam! I love how it looks like a painting!! Congrats on your ribbon!!!</td>', 'Great shot Cam! I love how it looks like a painting!! Congrats on your ribbon!!!', '2006-05-10 02:55:33.000000', NULL, 0),
