(2400491, 329353, 2490, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!<br/></td>', 'Congratulations!', '2006-05-10 09:07:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400505, 329005, 50674, '<td valign="top">A new personal best. Many congratulations, I know you are enjoying being in 7th heaven, may you stay there for a long time.<br/>Oh, and the shot is worthy of the 5th place it got. Marvelous colours in a very good composition.</td>', 'A new personal best. Many congratulations, I know you are enjoying being in 7th heaven, may you stay there for a long time.Oh, and the shot is worthy of the 5th place it got. Marvelous colours in a very good composition.', '2006-05-10 09:12:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400513, 329346, 30364, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote (yet again) but I did sneak a peek and one of the things I saw was this. I thought it might be JPR! I''m so dumb; I did not initially make the rotate call and spent a moment wondering what kind of structure this could be, and why it had lights along one side.  I even wondered about the woman standing on tippy-toes, flattened against the wall!  The clever title held all the clues; I was just slow. <br/>The effect is to suggest a sort of sideways vertigo.  It''s another cerebral Dahkota photograph that makes some demands of the viewer (nearly too many for me, evidently).  And it''s not too dark on my 20" i-Mac, although the histogram makes interesting viewing; if the white point is moved to the "correct" position, the images loses some of its enigma, and so some of its point.  Better just where it is.</td>', 'Didn''t vote (yet again) but I did sneak a peek and one of the things I saw was this. I thought it might be JPR! I''m so dumb; I did not initially make the rotate call and spent a moment wondering what kind of structure this could be, and why it had lights along one side.  I even wondered about the woman standing on tippy-toes, flattened against the wall!  The clever title held all the clues; I was just slow. The effect is to suggest a sort of sideways vertigo.  It''s another cerebral Dahkota photograph that makes some demands of the viewer (nearly too many for me, evidently).  And it''s not too dark on my 20" i-Mac, although the histogram makes interesting viewing; if the white point is moved to the "correct" position, the images loses some of its enigma, and so some of its point.  Better just where it is.', '2006-05-10 09:14:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400529, 326943, 49652, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon.  Great idea and it''s got rhythm!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon.  Great idea and it''s got rhythm!', '2006-05-10 09:22:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400538, 329398, 43714, '<td valign="top">Way to go Rikki, great shot!</td>', 'Way to go Rikki, great shot!', '2006-05-10 09:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400545, 327006, 2490, '<td valign="top">[[Trading Post]]<br/> <br/>Others may disagree, but I like this lighting.  It does create a touch of a glare, but the shadows are still filled with detail and interest, and I think that is good.  It does fall a little short of making me think "rhythm" at first look.  I see what you''ve done and I think I understand the point, but the circular shape just doesn''t feel rhythmic, even though it is repetitious and continuous.  I would have probably given this a 6.</td>', '[[Trading Post]] Others may disagree, but I like this lighting.  It does create a touch of a glare, but the shadows are still filled with detail and interest, and I think that is good.  It does fall a little short of making me think "rhythm" at first look.  I see what you''ve done and I think I understand the point, but the circular shape just doesn''t feel rhythmic, even though it is repetitious and continuous.  I would have probably given this a 6.', '2006-05-10 09:27:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400552, 329005, 43714, '<td valign="top">Great job Shez!, wonderful image and colours. Congrats.</td>', 'Great job Shez!, wonderful image and colours. Congrats.', '2006-05-10 09:29:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400556, 329394, 48928, '<td valign="top">Amazing picture.  i really like the colors, reflections and silhoutte.</td>', 'Amazing picture.  i really like the colors, reflections and silhoutte.', '2006-05-10 09:31:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400558, 329346, 50695, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 10s. I think this is Best In Show.</td>', 'I was one of your 10s. I think this is Best In Show.', '2006-05-10 09:31:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400561, 328845, 43714, '<td valign="top">What a great shot, congrats! We missed you at the Toronto meet!<br/>Laurie</td>', 'What a great shot, congrats! We missed you at the Toronto meet!Laurie', '2006-05-10 09:33:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400562, 328905, 50695, '<td valign="top">You were robbed. I guess the DPCers just ain''t got that swing. They want the rhythm of a drum machine.</td>', 'You were robbed. I guess the DPCers just ain''t got that swing. They want the rhythm of a drum machine.', '2006-05-10 09:33:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400563, 327708, 2490, '<td valign="top">[[Trading Post]]<br/> <br/>OOOHH!  My first thought was "wicked cool", tempered by some of the flaws in the railings in the background.  There''s also a color shift to green as I see the flowers go from front to back, and it confuses me.  This is a great composition.  The background might be a bit too pure white for the rest of the photo.</td>', '[[Trading Post]] OOOHH!  My first thought was "wicked cool", tempered by some of the flaws in the railings in the background.  There''s also a color shift to green as I see the flowers go from front to back, and it confuses me.  This is a great composition.  The background might be a bit too pure white for the rest of the photo.', '2006-05-10 09:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400564, 329353, 326, '<td valign="top">Beautiful Image! I gave this a 10, nice work. Congratulations!</td>', 'Beautiful Image! I gave this a 10, nice work. Congratulations!', '2006-05-10 09:33:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400575, 326943, 43714, '<td valign="top">Very creative and colourful, congrats!</td>', 'Very creative and colourful, congrats!', '2006-05-10 09:39:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400582, 329353, 43714, '<td valign="top">Just beautiful, great job! Congrats</td>', 'Just beautiful, great job! Congrats', '2006-05-10 09:41:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400591, 329159, 2490, '<td valign="top">[[Trading Post]]<br/> <br/>For some reason this feels more like a fence than it does a piano.  There''s just no musical feeling.  It is a nice concept, but I''m not sure I like the true vertical lines, especially in multiples.</td>', '[[Trading Post]] For some reason this feels more like a fence than it does a piano.  There''s just no musical feeling.  It is a nice concept, but I''m not sure I like the true vertical lines, especially in multiples.', '2006-05-10 09:47:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400593, 328898, 2490, '<td valign="top">[[Trading Post]]<br/> <br/>You have done an excellent job with everything I see here - composition, color, exposure, processing, and so on.  I think your score only suffered because the subject isn''t intensely interesting.</td>', '[[Trading Post]] You have done an excellent job with everything I see here - composition, color, exposure, processing, and so on.  I think your score only suffered because the subject isn''t intensely interesting.', '2006-05-10 09:49:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400603, 329005, 4517, '<td valign="top">Terrific photo, very well done.</td>', 'Terrific photo, very well done.', '2006-05-10 09:54:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400661, 327708, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/> Very cool shot! The colors are great as is the focus. The only fault I can find is the very bright white of the background with the blow out in the top left corner (my left when looking at it). I didn''t vote this challenge but would have given it a 7.</td>', 'Trading post... Very cool shot! The colors are great as is the focus. The only fault I can find is the very bright white of the background with the blow out in the top left corner (my left when looking at it). I didn''t vote this challenge but would have given it a 7.', '2006-05-10 10:15:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400697, 327006, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  I see the rhythms in the line placement. This is a nice setup but not really eye catching. The things that could be improved (don''t take this the wrong way) would be using dishes that were newer looking, you can see the scratches at the bottom of the bowl as well as a small spot (or stain) on the side of the largest plate. Also, maybe a matching blue background. I didn''t score this challenge, but would have given you a 5.</td>', 'Trading post...  I see the rhythms in the line placement. This is a nice setup but not really eye catching. The things that could be improved (don''t take this the wrong way) would be using dishes that were newer looking, you can see the scratches at the bottom of the bowl as well as a small spot (or stain) on the side of the largest plate. Also, maybe a matching blue background. I didn''t score this challenge, but would have given you a 5.', '2006-05-10 10:22:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400698, 329353, 36606, '<td valign="top">fantastic photo! Congrats. Could we have an explantion on how u processed it please?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 09:23:19.</i></td>', 'fantastic photo! Congrats. Could we have an explantion on how u processed it please?', '2006-05-10 10:23:08.000000', '2006-05-10 10:23:19.000000', 0),
(2400710, 329159, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/> This is a neat image! I wouldn''t have guessed it to be a piano without the title. I like the tones of the wood. The focus is great. I think I would have liked it better if the lines were running horizontal with the nails at the top though. The shadows are very effective at adding to the rhythm.</td>', 'Trading post... This is a neat image! I wouldn''t have guessed it to be a piano without the title. I like the tones of the wood. The focus is great. I think I would have liked it better if the lines were running horizontal with the nails at the top though. The shadows are very effective at adding to the rhythm.', '2006-05-10 10:27:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400722, 327280, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  Awesome shot! Top 10 finish! Way to go dude! Obviously you don''t need any criticism on this shot. Perfect angle and lighting.</td>', 'Trading post...  Awesome shot! Top 10 finish! Way to go dude! Obviously you don''t need any criticism on this shot. Perfect angle and lighting.', '2006-05-10 10:31:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400724, 329141, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nice photo, subtle and well done on the finish.</td>', 'Nice photo, subtle and well done on the finish.', '2006-05-10 10:31:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400727, 328898, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  First let me say that you deserved a much higher score for this. Great perspective! I love the way it just vanishes into the sky. The colors are perfect. Great title tie in too. I would have given this a 9.</td>', 'Trading post...  First let me say that you deserved a much higher score for this. Great perspective! I love the way it just vanishes into the sky. The colors are perfect. Great title tie in too. I would have given this a 9.', '2006-05-10 10:34:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400734, 329415, 19670, '<td valign="top">This is a unique image--I gave it an 8. Go team!</td>', 'This is a unique image--I gave it an 8. Go team!', '2006-05-10 10:38:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2400760, 329141, 16241, '<td valign="top">nice nice nice!</td>', 'nice nice nice!', '2006-05-10 10:49:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401063, 326943, 41091, '<td valign="top">I don''t think this is a bad idea at all.  And obviously the DPC voters agree. congrats on a nice first place finish.</td>', 'I don''t think this is a bad idea at all.  And obviously the DPC voters agree. congrats on a nice first place finish.', '2006-05-10 12:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401069, 329353, 41091, '<td valign="top">This is a really cool perspective to use on this photo.  I take it it''s a reflection.  So, how many swampy areas did you have to wade/boat through to get into position for this shot?</td>', 'This is a really cool perspective to use on this photo.  I take it it''s a reflection.  So, how many swampy areas did you have to wade/boat through to get into position for this shot?', '2006-05-10 12:04:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401082, 329398, 41091, '<td valign="top">I actually like the crop, seeing as it would be the place where you have everything fastened together it probably isn''t as smooth and simple as the nice arch patterns you have going for you--which gives the image a lasting appeal.</td>', 'I actually like the crop, seeing as it would be the place where you have everything fastened together it probably isn''t as smooth and simple as the nice arch patterns you have going for you--which gives the image a lasting appeal.', '2006-05-10 12:08:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401144, 328845, 28710, '<td valign="top">Wicked awesome shot!<br/> <br/>Nice lighting, nice rhythm in the shot and fantastic capture of selected motion.<br/> <br/>Not to mention some FINE Irish ladies!<br/> <br/>Aye!</td>', 'Wicked awesome shot! Nice lighting, nice rhythm in the shot and fantastic capture of selected motion. Not to mention some FINE Irish ladies! Aye!', '2006-05-10 12:27:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401155, 326793, 28710, '<td valign="top">Great shot!<br/> <br/>I have an idea how difficult this is because I have toyed around with this sort of setup in the past. The first thing I saw in this pic was the lack of camera in the shot. That''s tricky! Mirrors can be really fiddly like this.<br/> <br/>I didn''t even notice the basket weave in the slinky, but after reading of it in your description, I noticed how great it looked alternately reversing in the mirrors too... very cool!<br/> <br/>At f/8, it looks like you may have encountered some softness inherent to diffraction limitation. Tough break shooting the P&amp;S on this one...<br/> <br/>That is one of the single greatest reasons I knew I had to get a DSLR.<br/> <br/>I find that on my S2 (which has a very similar pixel pitch and crop factor to the 8800), anything past f/5.6 starts to get a little soft... At f/7.1 and 8.0 it''s quite noticeable.<br/> <br/>I recently found a chart with hyperfocal distances for my camera and I think that will help a lot.<br/> <br/>Try a google... My hyperfocal distance can be as close as approx 5 meters (if I remember correctly) at f/5.6 which isn''t too bad with a bit of zoom...<br/> <br/>Something definitely worth researching as this can definitely help with shooting long DOF while keeping your diffraction effects at a minimum!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 11:38:01.</i></td>', 'Great shot! I have an idea how difficult this is because I have toyed around with this sort of setup in the past. The first thing I saw in this pic was the lack of camera in the shot. That''s tricky! Mirrors can be really fiddly like this. I didn''t even notice the basket weave in the slinky, but after reading of it in your description, I noticed how great it looked alternately reversing in the mirrors too... very cool! At f/8, it looks like you may have encountered some softness inherent to diffraction limitation. Tough break shooting the P&S on this one... That is one of the single greatest reasons I knew I had to get a DSLR. I find that on my S2 (which has a very similar pixel pitch and crop factor to the 8800), anything past f/5.6 starts to get a little soft... At f/7.1 and 8.0 it''s quite noticeable. I recently found a chart with hyperfocal distances for my camera and I think that will help a lot. Try a google... My hyperfocal distance can be as close as approx 5 meters (if I remember correctly) at f/5.6 which isn''t too bad with a bit of zoom... Something definitely worth researching as this can definitely help with shooting long DOF while keeping your diffraction effects at a minimum!', '2006-05-10 12:32:46.000000', '2006-05-10 12:38:01.000000', 0),
(2401166, 327280, 2490, '<td valign="top">[[Trading Post]]<br/> <br/>EXCLLENT use of light and congratulations on the finish!  Not really much critique to offer except that the sky color is a little bit dark; however, it still works very well.</td>', '[[Trading Post]] EXCLLENT use of light and congratulations on the finish!  Not really much critique to offer except that the sky color is a little bit dark; however, it still works very well.', '2006-05-10 12:36:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401180, 326943, 14476, '<td valign="top">Imaginative and excellent!  What more is there to say?<br/> <br/>Well done.</td>', 'Imaginative and excellent!  What more is there to say? Well done.', '2006-05-10 12:39:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401189, 329398, 14476, '<td valign="top">Keep up the **very good** work, Rikki.</td>', 'Keep up the **very good** work, Rikki.', '2006-05-10 12:41:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401216, 329350, 57631, '<td valign="top">Yes I know the crop is bad. The camera is a toy (Point and shoot auto everything, can''t really see the screen on a bright day.) Couldn''t tell the shot was even interesting till I got home, Never had another sunny day to reshoot.<br/> <br/>Border was an attempt to briing  the bright green, right center, in line with the grey green tonse of the background.</td>', 'Yes I know the crop is bad. The camera is a toy (Point and shoot auto everything, can''t really see the screen on a bright day.) Couldn''t tell the shot was even interesting till I got home, Never had another sunny day to reshoot. Border was an attempt to briing  the bright green, right center, in line with the grey green tonse of the background.', '2006-05-10 12:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401320, 329353, 49652, '<td valign="top">Congrats.  Beautiful.</td>', 'Congrats.  Beautiful.', '2006-05-10 13:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401327, 329398, 49652, '<td valign="top">Color and rhythm!  Very nice.  Congrats!</td>', 'Color and rhythm!  Very nice.  Congrats!', '2006-05-10 13:22:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401330, 329353, 42125, '<td valign="top">Please don''t leave us with: "Thanks all"<br/>Tell us how you did it!<br/>That is what DPC is all about.</td>', 'Please don''t leave us with: "Thanks all"Tell us how you did it!That is what DPC is all about.', '2006-05-10 13:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401363, 328696, 49652, '<td valign="top">This is very nice.  You have a really good eye.</td>', 'This is very nice.  You have a really good eye.', '2006-05-10 13:30:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401500, 328845, 58516, '<td valign="top">sweet deal!</td>', 'sweet deal!', '2006-05-10 13:58:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401631, 328402, 55199, '<td valign="top">These are the tuning pins on an autoharp, for those who wanted to know what the photo is of.</td>', 'These are the tuning pins on an autoharp, for those who wanted to know what the photo is of.', '2006-05-10 14:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401643, 329139, 40718, '<td valign="top">Before I looked at anything else I tried to guess the challenge and the score.  I was right on both, so I think you did well in meeting the challenge and 5.3 is on the high side of the pictures I comment on.  I could tell this was going to be there because it''s a fairly decent picture.  I also noticed even you didn''t predict a high score.<br/> <br/>1) It''s too dark.  If the front djembe could be as light as the back ones it would be a stronger picture.<br/> <br/>2) I''m torn about B&amp;W.  pictures which have a pattern or texture as their subject do well in B&amp;W, but I do like the rich brown you captured.<br/> <br/>3) Ultimately, although it is a nice picture and fit the challenge well, it has a tough time competing with other pictures which accomplish those two things but also have a subject with "wow".  By looking at your highest scoring pictures you already knew this...</td>', 'Before I looked at anything else I tried to guess the challenge and the score.  I was right on both, so I think you did well in meeting the challenge and 5.3 is on the high side of the pictures I comment on.  I could tell this was going to be there because it''s a fairly decent picture.  I also noticed even you didn''t predict a high score. 1) It''s too dark.  If the front djembe could be as light as the back ones it would be a stronger picture. 2) I''m torn about B&W.  pictures which have a pattern or texture as their subject do well in B&W, but I do like the rich brown you captured. 3) Ultimately, although it is a nice picture and fit the challenge well, it has a tough time competing with other pictures which accomplish those two things but also have a subject with "wow".  By looking at your highest scoring pictures you already knew this...', '2006-05-10 14:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401675, 327261, 56999, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone who voted and especially to those that left a comment, they were very helpful. A number of people have wondered what the thing is I imaged. It is a stainless steel splicing device used to attach two ends of a conveyor belt together.<br/> <br/>Thanks again;<br/> <br/>Danny<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-18 18:31:06.</i></td>', 'Thank you everyone who voted and especially to those that left a comment, they were very helpful. A number of people have wondered what the thing is I imaged. It is a stainless steel splicing device used to attach two ends of a conveyor belt together. Thanks again; Danny', '2006-05-10 14:41:32.000000', '2007-10-18 19:31:06.000000', 0),
(2401737, 329395, 24503, '<td valign="top">From the CTP MkII <br/> <br/>First Impression: Seems you where not right... it has worked well. A very nice shot that captures the viewer.<br/>Composition: Great. From right to left, from up and down to the center. It really creates a rhythm.<br/>Subject: curious, very curios indeed. It makes the viewer ask about what are you looking at.<br/>Technical: great focus and use of DOF. The colors are nice. The only flaw is the colour noise.<br/>Improvement: The sky is a bit blowed. IMO it would have worked better without the buildings (I know, they were there, you couldn''t help it...LOL). If the first man were looking at the camera this shot would have scored much better. The noise: it happens sometimes to me that set the camera to high levels of ISO and forget to correct them later.<br/>Summary: a really wonderful shot with some small flaws. Good job.<br/> <br/>Álex<br/></td>', 'From the CTP MkII  First Impression: Seems you where not right... it has worked well. A very nice shot that captures the viewer.Composition: Great. From right to left, from up and down to the center. It really creates a rhythm.Subject: curious, very curios indeed. It makes the viewer ask about what are you looking at.Technical: great focus and use of DOF. The colors are nice. The only flaw is the colour noise.Improvement: The sky is a bit blowed. IMO it would have worked better without the buildings (I know, they were there, you couldn''t help it...LOL). If the first man were looking at the camera this shot would have scored much better. The noise: it happens sometimes to me that set the camera to high levels of ISO and forget to correct them later.Summary: a really wonderful shot with some small flaws. Good job. Álex', '2006-05-10 14:55:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401740, 328656, 56673, '<td valign="top">I am very surprised by the scoring on this shot.  I gave it an "8" (very high for me) because I felt it really evoked a mood.</td>', 'I am very surprised by the scoring on this shot.  I gave it an "8" (very high for me) because I felt it really evoked a mood.', '2006-05-10 14:55:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401773, 329284, 56673, '<td valign="top">It took my kids to tell me that both people and even the dog are in step together.  The b/w and grain makes it feel like a cloudy/foggy day at the beach.  Nice mood.  (I had you at "6").</td>', 'It took my kids to tell me that both people and even the dog are in step together.  The b/w and grain makes it feel like a cloudy/foggy day at the beach.  Nice mood.  (I had you at "6").', '2006-05-10 15:01:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401813, 327783, 30454, '<td valign="top">That is creative. I wondered how it was done. From where you guys come up with this kind of ideas!! Now, I would definately like to try this technique, it kinda cool.</td>', 'That is creative. I wondered how it was done. From where you guys come up with this kind of ideas!! Now, I would definately like to try this technique, it kinda cool.', '2006-05-10 15:11:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2401959, 326943, 22689, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club :</b> <br/> <br/>Congrats for your first ribbon ! A blue one , that''s great !<br/> <br/>First things that came to my mind when I saw your photo were : original , very creative.That''s something I value because the elements you used are easy to find ; the way you have used them , your idea , was very good.<br/>All is in focus , it''s colorful , it''s pleasant to see.<br/> <br/>To improve it ? well , hard to say , maybe less noise in the sky (surely due to the unsharp mask and sharpening).<br/> <br/>Enjoy it , Tim !<br/> <br/>(Please feel free to email me for anything related with this critique)<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club :  Congrats for your first ribbon ! A blue one , that''s great ! First things that came to my mind when I saw your photo were : original , very creative.That''s something I value because the elements you used are easy to find ; the way you have used them , your idea , was very good.All is in focus , it''s colorful , it''s pleasant to see. To improve it ? well , hard to say , maybe less noise in the sky (surely due to the unsharp mask and sharpening). Enjoy it , Tim ! (Please feel free to email me for anything related with this critique)', '2006-05-10 15:42:28.000000', NULL, 0),
