(2413177, 329294, 41337, '<td valign="top">Comment: <br/><b>Greetings from the Critique Club... </b> <br/> <br/>The subject you chose fits the challenge pretty well. Technically, it''s hard to critique this photo since you ran a solarizing filter on it. Personally, I would have not done that for a challenge entry as that singlehandedly got you all those low votes. And that''s a shame because it looks like you had some good detail and the use of a wide angle really added unique interest to an otherwise common object.</td>', 'Comment: Greetings from the Critique Club...   The subject you chose fits the challenge pretty well. Technically, it''s hard to critique this photo since you ran a solarizing filter on it. Personally, I would have not done that for a challenge entry as that singlehandedly got you all those low votes. And that''s a shame because it looks like you had some good detail and the use of a wide angle really added unique interest to an otherwise common object.', '2006-05-14 00:01:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2413378, 329395, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Nice shot. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Composition is good. The flag the guy is holding up the face is very distracting and takes everything away for the picture and theme of rhythm.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Not the best subject for this challenge.<br/>Technical (Colour and light): <br/>Good color, lighting and DOF. Building in the back is little bit blown out. <br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>Better composition and timing. I think you did not shot this picture with the rhythm in mind. I would have avoided the building in the back and just took the people for the rhythm shot.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Congratulations on your PB, I am sure you are on right track and this will not stay your Personal best for long.<br/> <br/>Best of luck for the future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. First Impression Nice shot. Composition: Composition is good. The flag the guy is holding up the face is very distracting and takes everything away for the picture and theme of rhythm.Subject: Not the best subject for this challenge.Technical (Colour and light): Good color, lighting and DOF. Building in the back is little bit blown out. Improvement: Better composition and timing. I think you did not shot this picture with the rhythm in mind. I would have avoided the building in the back and just took the people for the rhythm shot.Summary: Congratulations on your PB, I am sure you are on right track and this will not stay your Personal best for long. Best of luck for the future challenges.', '2006-05-14 01:18:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2413663, 326943, 44058, '<td valign="top">well done!!!</td>', 'well done!!!', '2006-05-14 03:41:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2413750, 329286, 41337, '<td valign="top">Comment: <br/><b>Greetings from the Critique Club... </b> <br/> <br/>Nice image for the Rhythm Challenge. Compositionally this works. What I might do next time is crop a bit tigher so you don''t have that white space in the corner. In regards to the DOF, it looks good, however it appears you sharpened that area a bit too much especially the top of the key so I''d try and avoid that in the future. <br/> <br/>Other than that there isn''t much else I''d change. Maybe make the white keys whiter so they provide more contrast with the black keys.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-14 03:54:53.</i></td>', 'Comment: Greetings from the Critique Club...   Nice image for the Rhythm Challenge. Compositionally this works. What I might do next time is crop a bit tigher so you don''t have that white space in the corner. In regards to the DOF, it looks good, however it appears you sharpened that area a bit too much especially the top of the key so I''d try and avoid that in the future.  Other than that there isn''t much else I''d change. Maybe make the white keys whiter so they provide more contrast with the black keys.', '2006-05-14 04:53:03.000000', '2006-05-14 04:54:53.000000', 0),
