(2414653, 328652, 22689, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club :</b> <br/> <br/>Hi John ,<br/> <br/>I''ve noticed that you registered here last month : welcome !<br/>I like this place very much and I hope you''ll find here nice people and good advices/tips.<br/>Still few photos in your portfolio , <i>baby_girl.jpg</i> is really nice ! Great work of edition !<br/> <br/>Back to your challenge entry , the idea was good but maybe not for a Rhythm challenge (description : Repeat a theme to create rhythm in your photograph) , the "waves" of the cola created a too subtle rhythm , there are too many bright reflections and those highlights are a bit disturbing.Another point is the focus , the main subject is blurry , focus seems to be centered only on the rim.<br/>I don''t know what was your goal with this photo , maybe without the rim , in a bigger container , it would have appeared more abstract.<br/> <br/>I have had a look at your web site , I''m sure that soon I''ll see your entries in the top 20 (at least).<br/> <br/>Please feel free to email me about this critique.<br/>(I''m an amateur and this is only my opinion.)<br/> <br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club :  Hi John , I''ve noticed that you registered here last month : welcome !I like this place very much and I hope you''ll find here nice people and good advices/tips.Still few photos in your portfolio , baby_girl.jpg is really nice ! Great work of edition ! Back to your challenge entry , the idea was good but maybe not for a Rhythm challenge (description : Repeat a theme to create rhythm in your photograph) , the "waves" of the cola created a too subtle rhythm , there are too many bright reflections and those highlights are a bit disturbing.Another point is the focus , the main subject is blurry , focus seems to be centered only on the rim.I don''t know what was your goal with this photo , maybe without the rim , in a bigger container , it would have appeared more abstract. I have had a look at your web site , I''m sure that soon I''ll see your entries in the top 20 (at least). Please feel free to email me about this critique.(I''m an amateur and this is only my opinion.) ', '2006-05-14 15:45:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2414778, 327708, 14414, '<td valign="top"><i>trading post</i> <br/> <br/>I''m not really sure what i''m looking at here... and this puts me off a little. I get that its mirrors, with a repeated reflection, but I still keep trying to figure out how the metal bars all fit in...lol I think it works compositionally, but I personally get distracted by trying to figure out what''s what.<br/> <br/>The rhythm of the repetition works well, but I get a kind of clinical feel from it, I think from the greens of the sheets, and the metal bars. <br/> <br/>It is quite busy, I think it may work better with a lower angle, and cropping out the bars in the top half so that it is simpler, and the reflections recede further into the distance.</td>', 'trading post  I''m not really sure what i''m looking at here... and this puts me off a little. I get that its mirrors, with a repeated reflection, but I still keep trying to figure out how the metal bars all fit in...lol I think it works compositionally, but I personally get distracted by trying to figure out what''s what. The rhythm of the repetition works well, but I get a kind of clinical feel from it, I think from the greens of the sheets, and the metal bars.  It is quite busy, I think it may work better with a lower angle, and cropping out the bars in the top half so that it is simpler, and the reflections recede further into the distance.', '2006-05-14 17:10:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2414793, 327280, 14414, '<td valign="top"><i>~trading post~</i> <br/> <br/>This is a great photo, ,and i think you''ve composed it perfectly, with the different angles and the slight off-centredness of the main corner. The colours of the sky and building complement each other well, but the sky seems a little dark, and flat. <br/>Personally I''d prefer a touch less contrast on the building, so that the bottom front is not so blown-out.<br/> <br/>Congrats on the placing, and an awesome photo for the challenge,</td>', '~trading post~  This is a great photo, ,and i think you''ve composed it perfectly, with the different angles and the slight off-centredness of the main corner. The colours of the sky and building complement each other well, but the sky seems a little dark, and flat. Personally I''d prefer a touch less contrast on the building, so that the bottom front is not so blown-out. Congrats on the placing, and an awesome photo for the challenge,', '2006-05-14 17:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
